          "title": "Prefill vs Decode: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Phases",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Prefill",
                "Decode"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Tokens per pass",
                  "whole prompt",
                  "one token"
                ],
                [
                  "Bound by",
                  "{orange:compute}",
                  "{blue:memory bandwidth}"
                ],
                [
                  "Cache",
                  "fills KV cache",
                  "reads KV cache + weights"
                ],
                [
                  "Sets",
                  "TTFT",
                  "TPOT"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Prefill is one ==parallel== forward pass",
                "Decode reads ==all weights== every step",
                "Each token needs the previous: ==no parallelism== in one request"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Loop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Queue",
                    "sub": "wait",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Prefill",
                    "sub": "prompt",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1st token",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Decode",
                    "sub": "repeat",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Latency Maths",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==TTFT== ≈ queue wait + prefill time",
                "==TPOT== = one decode step",
                "Long prompt hurts TTFT; long output hurts total"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Total latency",
              "text": "==TTFT + (N − 1) × TPOT==, N = output tokens"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is decode memory-bound?** One token per pass, little compute per weight read",
                "**What lowers TTFT?** Shorter prompts, less queue wait"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The KV Cache",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The KV Cache",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Cache",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Attention needs ==K and V of every previous token==",
                "Cached, so no prefix recompute per decode step"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cache Size",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Per token = ==2 × layers × KV heads × head dim × bytes==",
                "Grows **linearly** with sequence length and batch size"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Llama-2-7B, FP16",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Layers × KV heads × head dim",
                  "32 × 32 × 128"
                ],
                [
                  "Bytes per value",
                  "2"
                ],
                [
                  "Per token",
                  "≈ 0.5 MB"
                ],
                [
                  "4k-token sequence",
                  "≈ 2 GB"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shrink It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:GQA / MQA}: query heads share KV heads, cache several times smaller",
                "{purple:Paged attention} (vLLM): fixed-size blocks, no fragmentation, prefix sharing"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Weights-only sizing",
              "text": "The ==KV cache==, not the weights, often caps batch size and context length."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why cache K and V?** Skips prefix recompute each step.",
                "**Why does GQA help?** Fewer KV heads, smaller cache.",
                "**Why page the cache?** No fragmentation, shared prefixes."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Batching and Continuous Batching",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Batching and Continuous Batching",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Batch",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Decode is ==memory-bound==: each step reads all weights",
                "Batching shares **one weight read** across many requests",
                "Throughput rises ==almost free=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Static vs Continuous",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Static",
                "Continuous"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Schedules",
                  "whole batch",
                  "every token step"
                ],
                [
                  "Finished request",
                  "idles behind longest",
                  "{green:leaves}, slot freed"
                ],
                [
                  "New request",
                  "waits for next batch",
                  "{green:joins} immediately"
                ],
                [
                  "GPU slots",
                  "{red:wasted}",
                  "kept full"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Chunked Prefill and Limits",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Chunked prefill==: long prompt split into pieces, mixed with decode steps",
                "One big prompt no longer stalls **other users' tokens**",
                "Bigger batch: more throughput, but ==higher per-request latency== and KV cache use"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Batch cap",
              "text": "Set by ==GPU memory== (KV cache) and the **latency target**."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why does batching help decode?** One weight read serves many requests.",
                "**Static vs continuous?** Continuous swaps requests every token step.",
                "**Why chunk prefill?** Protects other users' token latency."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
